WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.080
Series Robo Supermax my giant friend. Season one episode one

00:05.480 --> 00:11.000
Ever pondered why your favorite toy robot can move and talk on its own well dear friend

00:11.040 --> 00:13.440
We're about to unravel this mystery together

00:14.080 --> 00:18.440
Welcome to the fascinating world of robotics a realm where science and imagination

00:19.160 --> 00:23.800
Intertwine you see a robot isn't just a collection of metal parts and wires

00:24.080 --> 00:29.600
It's a marvel of engineering and programming a testament to the human brains ingenuity

00:30.000 --> 00:32.720
At its core a robot is an automated machine

00:33.480 --> 00:37.760
Capable of performing tasks independently often mimicking human actions

00:38.000 --> 00:44.360
It's the science behind how it functions that truly makes it captivating take computer programming for instance

00:44.520 --> 00:51.800
This is the secret language that instructs your robot on what to do and when to do it now add sensors into the mix

00:52.000 --> 00:56.440
These act like our senses helping the robot to interact with its environment

00:56.720 --> 01:01.680
So the magic behind your toy robots movements and chatter is not magic at all

01:01.880 --> 01:08.720
But science now that we know what makes a robot tick. How about we delve a little deeper into the science behind it

01:09.640 --> 01:16.580
imagine a robot as a multifaceted machine a blend of physics electronic circuits and computer science

01:17.080 --> 01:23.640
Intriguing isn't it first? Let's talk physics the motors inside a robot are like the muscles in our bodies

01:23.880 --> 01:28.280
They help robots move around just as muscles help us walk or run

01:28.920 --> 01:32.920
Next we have electronic circuits the lifeblood of a robot

01:33.200 --> 01:39.100
These circuits channel power to different parts of the robot much like our veins carry blood to our organs

01:39.720 --> 01:46.000
Finally we step into the realm of computer science. This is where the magic happens the programming

01:46.720 --> 01:51.240
Programming is like the brain of the robot giving it instructions on what to do

01:51.560 --> 01:55.400
So physics is the muscle circuits are the veins and

01:56.100 --> 02:01.160
Programming is the brain together. They bring our robotic friends to life and

02:01.680 --> 02:08.120
There you have it the science that powers our incredible robotic friends with all this talk about robots

02:08.280 --> 02:11.160
Have you ever wondered how they affect our everyday lives?

02:11.960 --> 02:16.040
Well, let's take a moment to appreciate the marvels of robotics

02:16.560 --> 02:22.920
Robots aren't just characters in your favorite anime or science fiction movie. They're real and they're here

02:23.480 --> 02:25.880
transforming the way we live work and play

02:26.920 --> 02:33.680
consider the medical field where robots perform complex surgeries with precision that surpasses human capabilities or

02:34.120 --> 02:39.600
Think about space exploration where robots brave the harsh unknown territories of outer space

02:40.160 --> 02:43.640
Gathering valuable data and unlocking the mysteries of the universe

02:44.120 --> 02:49.880
These aren't just robots. They're pioneers surgeons explorers and so much more

02:50.400 --> 02:57.260
By delving into the fascinating world of robotics you open doors to a future filled with exciting career opportunities

02:57.640 --> 03:03.120
From designing robots to programming them the possibilities are as vast as your imagination

03:03.440 --> 03:08.640
So next time you play with your toy robot, remember you're holding a piece of the future in your hands

